    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1464">

                <pb facs="1381" n="1215" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg1215"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 816.48/8</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Long to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">San Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-06-10T11:00:00-05:56">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 10, 1917, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I communicated to President Melendez in appropriate terms the purpose of your
                    plain cable of ninth. He expressed deep appreciation, but thought Salvador could
                    deal with situation for the present. He stated that he would riot hesitate to
                    call upon us for laid should it become necessary.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Long</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
